      "problem": "A car rental agency charges a fixed fee of $$25$ plus $$0.08$ per mile for the rental of a particular car.\n\nWhat expression gives the total cost, in dollars, if the car is driven for  $m$ miles?",
      "worked_solution": "If $m$ is the number of miles that the car is driven, and the car rental agency charges a fee of $$0.08$ per mile, then the cost for $m$ miles must be $0.08m.$ \n\nThere is also a fixed fee of $$25.$ Consequently, the constant term of the expression should be $25.$\n\nTherefore, the expression that represents the total cost (in dollars) when the car is driven for  $m$ miles must be \n\n$$\n0.08m+25\n$$",
